findings.detail:
src/lib/events/eventDetail.ts:210-215 (verified at HEAD, main):
```
const name = event.name?.[0]?.string ?? series?.name?.[0]?.string ?? '';
const durationMinutes =
	event.duration_minutes?.[0]?.number ?? series?.duration_minutes?.[0]?.number ?? 0;
const location = event.location?.[0]?.string ?? series?.default_location?.[0]?.string ?? '';
const description =
	event.description?.[0]?.string ?? series?.default_description?.[0]?.string ?? '';
```
Four fields inherit: name←series.name, durationMinutes←series.duration_minutes, location←series.default_location, description←series.default_description. `eventType`/`startDatetime` never inherit (module doc + type comments say so explicitly).

The has-no-own-value test is `??` chained on `event.<prop>?.[0]?.<slot>` — it fires only when the event's property ARRAY IS ABSENT/EMPTY (so `.[0]` is undefined), NOT when a stored value is falsy. A stored `duration_minutes: 0` or `location: ''`/`description: ''` on the event is a real (non-nullish) value and blocks inheritance even though it displays as blank/zero — this is called out explicitly in the code's own comments (+page.svelte:1992-2015, `draftWireValue`'s doc): writing an empty string or 0 back to the event PERMANENTLY MASKS the series default rather than restoring inheritance, because `??` doesn't treat `''`/`0` as nullish. So issue #304's 'fields THIS event actually inherits' computation must replicate exactly this test — check `event.<rawProp>` array presence/length, not the merged displayed value's truthiness — to correctly list which of the four fields are inherited for a given event.

seriesId is NOT currently exposed on the `EventDetail` type (only `seasonId` is, at eventDetail.ts:65-73/262-267) — internally computed at line 200 (`const seriesId = parents.find((p) => p.entity_type === 'event_series')?.reference ?? '';`) but discarded from the return object. A series picker needs this added to the contract to know which series is currently assigned and to compute the four raw event.<field> presences for the inheritance-preview.
